      "text": "To solve this problem, we need to find the area of the shaded region in the given logo and then determine what percentage of the area of the square this shaded region represents.\n\nFirst, let's analyze the logo structure. The square has a side length of 20 inches, and inside this square, there are four quarter-circles of radius 1 inch each, and each quarter-circle is tangent to two sides of the square and its two adjacent circles.\n\n1. **Calculate the area of the square:**\n   The area of the square is given by:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Area of the square} = 20 \\times 20 = 400 \\text{ square inches}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the area of one quarter-circle:**\n   The radius of each quarter-circle is 1 inch. The area of a full circle with radius 1 inch is:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Area of a full circle} = \\pi \\times 1^2 = \\pi \\text{ square inches}\n   \\]\n   Since each quarter-circle is one-fourth of a full circle, the area of one quarter-circle is:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Area of one quarter-circle} = \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\text{ square inches}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the total area of the four quarter-circles:**\n   There are four quarter-circles, so the total area of the four quarter-circles is:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total area of the four quarter-circles} = 4 \\times \\frac{\\pi}{4} = \\pi \\text{ square inches}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Calculate the shaded area:**\n   The shaded area is the area of the square minus the total area of the four quarter-circles:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Shaded area} = 400 - \\pi \\text{ square inches}\n   \\]\n\n5. **Calculate the percentage of the shaded area relative to the area of the square:**\n   The percentage of the shaded area is given by:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Percentage of shaded area} = \\left( \\frac{\\pi}{400} \\right) \\times 100 = \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\approx 0.7854 \\%\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the number of square inches that will be shaded is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{400 - \\pi}\n\\]",
