      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to determine the area of the shaded region in Wei's logo when the square is 20 inches on each side. \n\nFirst, let's analyze the geometric configuration of the logo. The square has a side length of 20 inches. Each circle is tangent to two sides of the square and its two adjacent circles. This means that the diameter of each circle is equal to the distance between the centers of two adjacent circles, which is twice the radius of the circle.\n\nThe distance between the centers of two adjacent circles is equal to the sum of their radii. Since the circles are tangent to the sides of the square, the distance from the center of each circle to the side of the square is equal to the radius of the circle. Therefore, the side length of each circle is equal to the radius of the circle.\n\nLet's denote the radius of each circle by \\( r \\). The distance between the centers of two adjacent circles is \\( 2r \\). This distance is also equal to the side length of the square minus the diameter of two circles (since the circles are tangent to each other and to the sides of the square).\n\nSo, we have:\n\\[ 2r = 20 - 2r \\]\nSolving for \\( r \\):\n\\[ 2r + 2r = 20 \\]\n\\[ 4r = 20 \\]\n\\[ r = 5 \\]\n\nThe radius of each circle is 5 inches. The area of one circle is:\n\\[ \\text{Area of one circle} = \\pi r^2 = \\pi (5)^2 = 25\\pi \\]\n\nSince there are four circles, the total area of the circles is:\n\\[ \\text{Total area of circles} = 4 \\times 25\\pi = 100\\pi \\]\n\nThe area of the square is:\n\\[ \\text{Area of the square} = 20 \\times 20 = 400 \\]\n\nThe shaded area is the area of the square minus the total area of the circles:\n\\[ \\text{Shaded area} = 400 - 100\\pi \\]\n\nTherefore, the number of square inches that will be shaded is:\n\\[ \\boxed{400 - 100\\pi} \\]",
