      "text": "To solve this problem, we need to determine the area of the logo Wei has designed and then find the fraction of this area that is shaded. The logo is a 4x4 square with 4 quarter circles at each corner, and 4 circles in between, each tangent to two sides of the square and its adjacent circles.\n\nFirst, let's calculate the area of the square. The side length of the square is 4 inches, so the area of the square is:\n\\[\n4 \\times 4 = 16 \\text{ square inches}\n\\]\n\nNext, we need to calculate the area of the four quarter circles. Each quarter circle has a radius of 1 inch (since the diameter of each circle is equal to the side length of the square minus twice the radius of the quarter circles, which gives us 1 inch per quarter circle). The area of one full circle with radius 1 inch is:\n\\[\n\\pi \\times 1^2 = \\pi \\text{ square inches}\n\\]\nSince each quarter circle is one-fourth of a full circle, the area of one quarter circle is:\n\\[\n\\frac{\\pi}{4} \\text{ square inches}\n\\]\nThere are four quarter circles, so the total area of the four quarter circles is:\n\\[\n4 \\times \\frac{\\pi}{4} = \\pi \\text{ square inches}\n\\]\n\nNow, the area of the shaded region is the area of the square minus the area of the four quarter circles:\n\\[\n16 - \\pi \\text{ square inches}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the number of square inches that will be shaded is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{16 - \\pi}\n\\]",
